Understand a transfer at the interface between two organisations (@cs-loading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME", #source "../sources/Cryogenic-Liquid-Tanker-Transfers-AIGA.lingua#r_52MNR8Y6S0N1MXDSX8F3XF424C", #source "../sources/Flammable-Liquid-Tanks-HSE-HSG176.lingua#r_3J96NXWJF945DTPAPBRQPT177R", #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #chemical-supply-systems "Custody-quantity-measurement-and-reconciliation.lingua#r_5YJA6RTG07SBRX9C6H2Q6YRDD4") { r_308YPHWHSV82M1F4BYZRBBV559
**Read:** [Caustic Soda Handbook — OxyChem](../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME), the complete unloading and equipment chapters; [Good practices guide for loading and unloading of cryogenic liquid tankers — AIGA](../sources/Cryogenic-Liquid-Tanker-Transfers-AIGA.lingua#r_52MNR8Y6S0N1MXDSX8F3XF424C), the full tanker-transfer guide; [Storage of flammable liquids in tanks — HSE HSG176](../sources/Flammable-Liquid-Tanks-HSE-HSG176.lingua#r_3J96NXWJF945DTPAPBRQPT177R), complete loading/unloading and operating sections; [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), the complete dispatch, transport and contract sections.

Follow an actual loading/unloading operation as a sequence of defined states and responsibilities. Identify source and destination, material/grade, available receiving capacity, equipment/contact history, connections, measurement, communications and completion evidence. The bulk material should remain tied to its identity and quality history across the interface.

Read the complete product-specific unloading chapters and the relevant general storage guide. Compare a tanker delivery with packaged receiving, and a cryogenic transfer with a near-atmospheric liquid. Determine which features are specific to pressure, temperature, reactivity or product cleanliness. Do not construct an operating procedure by combining isolated instructions from incompatible service domains.

Build a documentary transfer analysis that names both parties' information needs before, during and after the movement. Include residuals, sample ownership, measured quantities, status of the receiving material and a deviation scenario. Compare how responsibility is allocated in direct and contracted logistics. The outcome should identify the evidence and competent work necessary to qualify the operation; literary reconstruction or a mass-balance calculation must be labelled accordingly. Later detailed equipment and operating studies deepen the physical methods without obscuring this cross-party interface.

**Continue:** [Reconcile quantities across a material transfer](Custody-quantity-measurement-and-reconciliation.lingua#r_5YJA6RTG07SBRX9C6H2Q6YRDD4).

